WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.210
Friendship

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.370
thief

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.370
parent and child crooks

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.100
<b>Episode 9: Hurry Up and "Switch Sides"</b>

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.480
Switch sides?

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.220
<b>Episode 9: Hurry Up and "Switch Sides"</b>

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.220
What the hell is he saying?!

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:39.570
I-It's got to be a bluff! There's no 
way he's serious about switching.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.450
I wonder about that.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.010
I tend to think Katagiri Yuichi 
would be comfortable

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.620
doing something like that 
to achieve his goal.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:52.490
So, if he honestly does want to 
switch sides, would you accept it?

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b>Third Game Rules</b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Can't Do</b></b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Violence</b></b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Moving the Hider</b></b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Can Do</b></b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Contact</b></b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Food</b></b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Surrender (Give Up)</b></b>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b><b>Change Sides (Switch)</b></b>

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.460
<b><b>Change Sides (Switch)</b></b>

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.410
Well, of course I would.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.780
If he joins our side, 
victory is all but inevitable.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.080
That's true, if you think 
about it... normally.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.910
If this goes the way I think it will, 
the game will really start to move

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.320
depending on if they accept
 Katagiri Yuichi's switch.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:14.730
Well? Will you allow me 
to switch sides or not?

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:20.280
Hmm. What made you want
 to switch sides now?

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.530
It's like I said...

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.280
<b>Bad-Mouth</b>

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.280
<b></b>Actually, Sawaragi Shiho 
has had plastic surgery.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.070
Tenji destroyed our friendships
in the second game.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.030
<b>Actually, Sawaragi Shiho 
has had plastic surgery.</b>

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.040
I decided to use the third game 
to make him suffer

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.960
as much as possible, and then switch sides.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.420
Well, I guess that tracks.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.130
Then hurry up and allow it. 
You remember how to do it, right?

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.260
<b>Things You Can Do</b>

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.260
<b>Change Sides (Switch)</b>

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.430
About switching sides,

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.450
I'll always be in the center 
area where the food is,

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.520
so come and make a formal announcement 
with someone from the other team.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.520
Is it okay if I switch sides?

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.520
If at least one person from 
the other team agrees, it's settled.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.520
Okay with me!!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.540
But be careful, because 
you can't switch again

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.780
Actually, can I come back?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.780
Screw off!

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.900
and go back to your original team.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.720
What do you think? 
I'm okay with letting him in.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.690
Usually, I'd never want 
a guy like this on our side.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.830
But to help us win? In that case...

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.410
M'kay, if there are no objections...

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.370
Hold on, please.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.440
Until now, whenever we
 had a choice to make,

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.460
we always asked Captain to decide.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.510
So, why don't we ask him 
now too, just to be safe?

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.470
Aw, it's fine. Why bother?

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.390
You asshole!

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.240
Captain's decisions are absolute!

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.770
He's the reason we've gotten this far!

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.180
I can't believe what I almost did!

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.480
Okay, fine, I get it.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.110
What? What do you think is so funny?

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:41.130
My bad. I didn't mean it.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.240
It's just...

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:49.240
It's ridiculous that you guys can't make 
a simple decision like this by yourselves.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:55.520
You can't seriously have been asking your 
precious Captain-sama's permission

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.380
for every single move up until this point?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.590
"Captain-sama, shall we go left or right?"

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:05.590
"Captain-sama, will we have bread 
or rice for breakfast?"

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.220
"Captain-sama, may I please go pee-pee?"

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.230
C'mon, how much of a control 
freak is your Captain, anyway?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.610
You piece of shit.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.820
Our Captain...

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:23.610
Our Captain... ain't like that at all!

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.540
Please don't be violent!

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:28.330
If you attack the other team, 
we'll immediately lose!

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.160
But this asshole...

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.960
Hyakutaro, calm down.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.370
We still have plenty of time.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.750
Banri-san... okay.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.070
For now, please stay here with Hyakutaro-senpai 
so he doesn't do anything rash.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.330
I'll go call him right away.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.190
Hello, is that you, Captain?

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.770
Phew, that was close!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.870
We almost lost over a stupid accident.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.030
Was it really an accident?

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:00.820
Huh?

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.900
Are you saying he was
 deliberately provoking him?

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.180
Gosh, who knows?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.080
But you might not want to take such 
a simplistic view of his actions.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.910
Well, either way, once Katagiri Yuichi 
switches sides, the game is over.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:20.670
Um, okay. I'll tell you Captain's decision.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:25.050
"I will not allow that Katagiri 
Yuichi guy to switch sides."

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.430
That's what he said.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.380
W-Why in the world not?!

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.930
No, that's probably the correct decision.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.050
"The reason is clear and simple."

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:37.390
"We'll definitely win even 
without him on our side."

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.270
"The strategy I thought up is flawless."

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.960
Strategy?

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:47.320
"So don't get distracted. Just trust me 
and carry out the plan," he said.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:51.880
"But if Katagiri Yuichi still 
insists on switching teams,"

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.830
"make the girl switch with him."

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:00.230
"If they both switch, Group C will 
be down to just the one hider."

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.560
"They wouldn't be able to 
pull any tricks, then."

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:08.200
"For example, if Katagiri Yuichi switched 
and started working with us,"

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:11.100
<b>I'd like to give my regards 
to your Captain!!</b>

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:11.100
<b>buttering up</b>

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.700
"he might trick us into 
telling him our hiding place."

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:13.630
"Then, he could tell the girl 
and send her to find him."

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.600
<b>I found him.</b>

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:16.060
"Katagiri Yuichi's debt would 
increase, but despite starting"

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.600
<b>Okay!</b>

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.600
"with such a huge disadvantage,"

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.360
<b>Victory</b>

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.590
"they would at least grab victory."

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:21.640
No kidding!

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.900
In that case, let's have 'em 
both switch over.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.780
You've got no reason to refuse, right?

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.240
You've got a grudge against Mikasa Tenji. 
That's why you're switching, right?

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:34.290
<i>My, oh my. The strategy was easier 
to see through than I thought.</i>

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.500
<i>Group K's leader is pretty sharp.</i>

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:45.590
<i>But too bad for them, since that 
was already part of this guy's plan.</i>

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.590
<b>Two Days Ago</b>

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.590
<b>Several Hours After the Start of the Third Game</b>

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:52.510
So what are we going to do, Yuichi-san?

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.570
Nothing, for at least
 for the next two full days.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:01.390
That'll give the impression that I have 
no intention of fighting them.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.660
Then on the third day,
 I'll announce I want to switch sides.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:05.900
Are you planning to betray us?

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:10.420
Of course not. I'm not thinking 
about anything except winning.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.950
<i>Huh... He's sticking to it, then.</i>

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:14.870
In other words,

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:18.830
I'm ready to do whatever it takes to win.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.660
<i>Wow! He really is something in the flesh!</i>

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.710
<i>That villainous look on his face!</i>

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:28.340
If I <i>am</i> able to switch, my plan is 
to get their hiding spot out of them,

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.650
and then tell you where it is.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.720
Oh, I see!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.850
But still, there's about a ten
to one chance this plan will fail.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.730
Huh? Why do you think so?

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:43.860
Because Group K has probably already 
figured out the strategy for this game.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:50.140
The only sure and simple way to find 
the other hider in Friendly Hide-and-Seek

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.860
<b>Food</b>

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.860
is to tail the other team 
when they deliver food.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.990
<i>So, he </i>has<i> already figured it out.</i>

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.870
That might be true,

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.370
but what makes you think our opponents 
are already aware of that strategy?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.830
If this was normal hide-and-seek,

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:07.130
who would you pick 
in Group K to be the hider?

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.860
I'd want to reduce the chances 
of being found as much as possible,

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.620
so the smallest...

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:13.600
Ah!

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.290
Right. They should have picked 
the smallest guy on the team to hide.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:22.850
But instead, of all people, they picked 
the one who's by far the biggest.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.230
That proves they've already realized it's 
not the same as regular hide-and-seek.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:31.740
They picked the guy who would be 
the most patient over a long fight.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:36.320
So if your plan to switch sides fails, 
what will you do next?

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.330
Before I tell you that,

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:42.060
I need to make sure of one thing.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.080
What is it?

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.850
I told you I'd do whatever 
it takes to win, right?

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:51.710
Will you go along with that?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.680
To get straight to the point,

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.030
will you swear your 
absolute obedience to me?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.380
<i>Does this guy think he's threatening me?</i>

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:10.140
<i>But hey, at least it's getting interesting!</i>

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:13.490
S-Sure, I will. As long as we win the game.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.860
Of course. If you follow my 
lead, we'll definitely win.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.820
<i>Wow, he's so confident!</i>

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:20.660
Okay, I'll tell you.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:31.710
<i>Oh, so that's why he asked 
if I was a girl earlier.</i>

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:35.720
<i>Even so, this guy, Katagiri Yuichi,</i>

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:40.200
<i>is even more of a crazy asshole 
than I thought!</i>

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.550
Well, what's the matter? 
Hurry up and switch.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.770
I don't have enough scenes 
in the third game...

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.790
Nah, I changed my mind about switching.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:53.670
Huh?!

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:55.760
Aw, why not?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.980
Was Captain spot-on about 
your strategy after all?

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.700
No, no, that isn't it.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.910
After watching you guys, 
I think it'll be an easy win.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.740
I figure we'll clean up here pretty quick.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.140
Give it your best shot.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:12.570
Back off, Hyakutaro.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.550
Shut it!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:17.420
Listen up. Here's the plan 
if I can't switch sides.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.630
I said I wouldn't do anything for the first 
two days, but that wasn't exactly true.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:24.630
I'll make small talk with the other team

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.020
You son of a...

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:27.690
and try to provoke them sometimes 
while I look for something.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.190
Bye-bye!

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.480
<b>Bye-bye!</b>

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.480
<b>Bye-bye!</b>

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:28.810
Something?

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:32.400
Once I find that thing, 
I'll move to the next step.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.930
<i>Once he finds it, it's fine,</i>

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:39.490
<i>but Tenji-kun's gotta be 
at his breaking point about now.</i>

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.490
<b>Third Game: Day 4</b>

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.490
<b>Early Morning</b>

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:50.090
We're going to bring Captain his breakfast,

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:52.300
so please take over the watch, guys.

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.000
Sure.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:11:00.440
<i>I say that, but they're both still 
dead asleep this morning, too.</i>

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:04.730
Hyakutaro.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:08.000
You sure aren't a morning person.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:11.490
Here. With plenty of sugar and milk.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.900
Oh!

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.980
This reminds me of our morning routine.

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:20.400
Sure does.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.780
That's right, you guys said you 
were in the basketball club.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.240
What the hell... You were awake?

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.200
Sorry. I guess it looks like 
I was eavesdropping.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.350
Hyakutaro, I'll keep an eye on the girl.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:34.040
Yeah, I got this.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:36.690
Have you been in basketball 
a while, Hyakutaro-kun?

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.390
Uh, yeah...

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.630
Hey, why you talkin' to me?

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.880
I can see how well you work together. 
You must be a really strong team.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.320
W-Well yeah, I guess!

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:48.560
We were totally headed 
for nationals this year.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:53.150
And that captain of yours is great! 
He's super sharp, but he's also huge!

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.400
What, so you <i>do</i> get it?!

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:59.130
Yeah, he's a really awesome guy!

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:00.820
But, y'know...

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.490
I kept making crappy shots 
and got Captain injured.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:13.320
So I trained my ass off to help 
him shine one last time.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:18.040
Huh. You really are just a 
wholesome, honest young man.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:22.920
But then, why'd you get stuck 
playing the Tomodachi Game?

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:27.180
Which one of you five is in debt?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.140
I-It's...

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.220
It's?

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:31.810
That's enough.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.810
Chisato!

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:37.590
Hyakutaro, let's trade spots 
before you say too much.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.320
S-Sorry.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:46.200
Phew. Back to the girl. Is—

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:48.660
Huh?

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:52.410
She was just sleeping here, right?

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:53.870
<i>Oh, shit!</i>

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.980
Damn it! She ran away!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:11.310
<b>Zing!</b>

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.480
Ah! I-I'm, uh, n-not... Th-This isn't...

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.060
I wasn't trying to...

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:25.380
Hyakutaro!

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.490
N-No...!

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.370
I-I-I didn't mean it!

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:31.270
What the hell are you doing?! 
Keep your eyes on her!

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.620
No! I mean, this is just, that...

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.170
Fine, then I'll go!

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:38.380
No, you can't, Chisato! Idiot! Perv!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.960
I found it! Maria!

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:43.380
Oh, no!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.800
Go after Yuichi! I'll follow Maria!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:46.760
G-Got it!

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.100
You ain't gettin' away!

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.400
Gotcha!

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:15.800
There they are!

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:16.550
This way!

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:17.770
Huh? Uh, okay!

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:18.770
Hyakutaro!

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:19.710
Yeah!

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:28.090
What he thought he "found" was a chance 
to split us up and then lose us.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.640
But we caught up anyway.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.100
Not a bad idea, but he was just out of luck.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.600
No, this is exactly what I planned.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:39.570
The thing I found is something else.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.190
Oops! My hand slipped!

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.130
Huh?!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.950
What?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.710
Mikasa Tenji

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.540
<i>I'm done for.</i>

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.210
<i>At this rate, I'll...</i>

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.480
<i>I've held on long enough, right?</i>

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.420
But what would change if I pushed it?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:26.400
Even if I escape this pain, I only have 
that empty life to return to.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.320
I said it, didn't I?

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:34.200
I will trust Yuichi 
no matter what happens.

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:39.160
Fine.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:41.500
I'll keep waiting like this...

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:46.960
and bet on Yuichi... 
on my last hope... with my life.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:54.980
I'm sorry, Dad, that I couldn't avenge you.

00:15:55.830 --> 00:16:02.180
I'm sorry, guys... that 
I couldn't... apologize directly.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:08.460
But at least I didn't betray 
anyone else at the end.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:11.120
I'm glad.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:23.670
Wh... What?

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.850
Tenji! Hold on, Tenji!

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.780
Yu...ichi...

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:31.600
Yuichi?!

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:32.640
Tenji!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.470
Yuichi! Yuichi!

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.410
Sorry to keep you waiting, Tenji.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.780
I'm back now.

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.440
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:48.850
Calorie Bar

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:46.240
So that's what happened.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:48.860
They would have tailed you 
if you brought food,

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:52.360
so you couldn't get back sooner.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:57.250
But you knew about that 
strategy from the start, right—

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:58.950
Well, yeah.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:07.500
If you told me that on the first day, 
I wouldn't have had to suffer so much.

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:11.380
Sorry. I did that on purpose, to test you.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:15.760
To see if you'd push the give-up button 
when you were in real trouble.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:19.430
If you pushed it, the game would end. 
We'd lose everything.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:24.100
But if you didn't, I decided 
I'd start to trust you again.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:27.370
Yuichi, you're an idiot.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:30.510
If I had no self-control 
and pushed the button...

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.850
If I started to resent you 
and simply pushed the button,

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:34.240
what were you going to do?!

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.820
You didn't push it, though.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:41.530
You risked your life to keep your promise,
and didn't push the button.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.610
Honestly, that makes me happy.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:46.500
The Tenji I knew in school 
wasn't a complete lie.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.330
Thanks, Tenji, for trusting me.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.880
From now on I'll really trust you, too.

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.380
<b>Mackerel</b>

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.390
Yuichi...

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:02.240
After you've lost something, 
it's so hard to get it back.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.010
I know it is.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:11.040
But trusting you doesn't necessarily 
mean I distrust Sawaragi 100 percent.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:14.400
Once we get back, we've got 
to get to the bottom of it all.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:16.470
That's good enough for me.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.160
So, what's going on?

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:23.160
Does it look like we can win?

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:24.790
We're in good shape.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:28.410
The fact that I made it back here means 
the plan is already halfway to success.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.740
How did you lose the Group K guys, anyway?

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.030
Yeah... by now,

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.600
they're probably saying 
all sorts of crap about me.

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:40.870
God damn that asshole!

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.890
Seriously, what's wrong with him?

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.520
Hey, you okay?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:49.280
Huh? Uh, yes, I'm all right.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:51.330
<i>Ooh, that was terrifying.</i>

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:55.440
<i>He did say he was going to use me 
as a distraction somehow.</i>

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:57.250
<i>What the...</i>

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.950
<i>Is this what he... meant as a...</i>

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.710
<i>distraction?!</i>

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.410
I'm going after him!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:09.000
No way! I can't pull her up by myself!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.150
Don't be stupid!

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:12.500
If she falls from that height, 
she won't be that hurt—

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.570
The hell she won't! Are you just 
gonna let a girl get hurt?

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:20.360
You're always chasin' girls, but you won't 
help one that's right in front of you?!

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.650
Fine! I'll help!

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:26.010
<i>Wow!</i>

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:28.040
Yeah, the Chisato I know 
wouldn't leave a girl hanging.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:30.520
<i>The method wasn't the best, but he
 really did slow them both down!</i>

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.520
Shut up and help pull!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.670
That's awful.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:34.360
Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:38.090
It was a really risky gamble to try that.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:39.820
It wasn't a gamble at all.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.680
I knew I just needed 
to slow one of them down.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:47.040
If one stopped, it was highly 
likely the other would, too.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.620
What do you mean? What made you think that?

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:54.110
I didn't just use my time these 
three days trying to wear you down.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:58.410
I was also observing the personalities 
and relationships in Group K.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.920
Sometimes I spilled a little info 
to get them talking,

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:04.470
other times I'd step up and provoke them.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:08.140
Eventually, I was able to find the thing—

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:10.510
or rather, the <i>person</i> I was searching for.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:12.980
It was Onigawara Hyakutaro.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:16.480
At first, he seems like 
a short-tempered and impulsive jerk,

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:18.510
but he's more compassionate
 than the others,

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:21.280
and is really self-conscious 
about past mistakes.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:24.360
On top of that, he's weirdly naïve 
and kind to girls.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:28.740
Yeah, the thing I was searching for 
was the kindest person in the group.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:31.890
He does sound like the type 
to try to save her,

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.900
but wasn't one other guy chasing, too?

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:38.350
The other guy, Hashiratani Chisato, 
was always paying attention to Hyakutaro.

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:39.170
Huh?

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:43.200
He reacted to almost everything 
Hyakutaro did and said.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:48.830
Chisato's kind of personality is what 
you'd call, in a word, a dilettante.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:45.430
<b>Bye-bye!</b>

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:45.430
<b>Bye-bye!</b>

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:52.130
You know, a jack of all trades, 
but master of none.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:55.440
When that type of person meets 
someone who's really sincere,

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.510
he might mouth off a lot, but deep inside, 
he's actually really jealous.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:02.320
<i>I think I know what he means.</i>

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:06.820
So when Hyakutaro seriously asks for help, 
it's hard for Chisato to turn him down.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.690
People who put so much effort 
into crafting a fake personality

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:12.830
can't stand it when more 
authentic people tell it like it is.

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:16.280
<i>What incredible analytical skills!</i>

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:20.300
<i>But he's almost </i>too<i> good at seeing through 
other people's personality flaws...</i>

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:23.310
Still, how is that helping us win?

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:26.750
It doesn't sound like 
we're halfway there to me.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:29.920
We are, and what's coming up 
is actually my specialty.

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:31.060
Your specialty?

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.850
<b>Kadokura Juzo</b>

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.850
<b>Onigawara Hyakutaro</b>

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.850
<b>Shinomiya Kei</b>

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.850
<b>Niwa Banri</b>

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.850
<b>Hashiratani Chisato</b>

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:35.850
The biggest hurdle was figuring out 
if my relationship analysis was accurate.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:39.360
That was already proven correct this time.

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:43.650
Now that I was able to bring you food, 
we have a little more time.

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:46.520
We only have to do one more thing to win...

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:52.040
Totally destroy all the
relationships in Group K.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.040
<b>Totally destroy them</b>

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.040
<b>Totally destroy them</b>

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:58.920
Over the last three days, 
I've already planted all sorts of traps.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:02.280
The first one will be set 
in motion any minute now.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:06.370
U-Um, thank you so much.

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:08.190
You saved my life.

00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:09.720
H-Huh? <i>I</i> did?

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:12.850
<i>Ooh, this is getting interesting!</i>

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:17.080
<i>Yuichi went back to Group K's camp.</i>

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.360
<i>I can't begin to imagine 
what he's done since then.</i>

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.860
Wait a second! What are you thinking?

00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:25.470
Shut up! I made up my mind!

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:27.120
Just calm down!

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:29.490
What are you guys doing? 
Did you eat something funny?

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:28.270
Let go of me!

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:30.970
Don't do it, Hyakutaro!

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:34.500
I know you don't give a 
damn about how I feel!

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.260
Manabu!

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:36.080
Huh?

00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:38.640
I'm switchin' to Group C!

00:22:39.310 --> 00:22:44.980
<i>The bonds holding Group K together 
crumbled in just one day.</i>

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:49.880
<b>NEXT: The Third Game Is Over!</b>
